# Generation. Without a key the harness uses an offline fixture provider that
# returns real, exportable Manim -- enough to exercise export, preview and the
# edit loop with no network.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-6-astra
# A model that reads images (empty: OPENROUTER_MODEL): the fallback for finding where a picture's labels go and for
# looking at a lecture's frames. (OPENROUTER_SVG_MODEL, its older name, still works.)
OPENROUTER_FIGURE_MODEL=
# The illustration model: people, places, objects, scenes, and the picture of each thing a diagram's node, a map's
# icon or a panel's line shows, as cutouts (on OpenRouter; if it refuses, the log says why). Nothing
# is drawn as an SVG.
# PANIM_IMAGE_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash-image
# The model for detailed diagrams (empty: PANIM_IMAGE_MODEL): the book's diagrams redrawn in the lecture's style
# from the figure itself, every label kept and checked, a script's detailed diagrams (draw), and pictures with
# labelled parts. It must take a picture in
# (OpenRouter "image" input) and write words well, e.g. google/gemini-3-pro-image-preview.
# PANIM_DIAGRAM_MODEL=
# Fallbacks (none by default): models asked in order when the model refuses a picture or its content filter blocks
# it ("The response was filtered due to the prompt triggering ... content management policy"). Comma-separated.
# A filtered picture is first asked again in plainer words; only then the fallbacks. A diagram fallback must take a
# picture in, e.g. google/gemini-3-pro-image-preview.
# PANIM_DIAGRAM_FALLBACK_MODELS=
# PANIM_IMAGE_FALLBACK_MODELS=
# Every figure of an uploaded book is redrawn by it as an exact copy in the lecture's style (the book's own pictures
# are never shown). PANIM_DIAGRAM_TRIES (4): tries at a redraw whose labels are not all right; then the closest is
# kept. PANIM_FIGURE_WAIT_SECONDS (420): how long the script waits for the redraws.
# The model that finds where a picture's labelled parts are (reads images; empty: OPENROUTER_FIGURE_MODEL).
# PANIM_LABEL_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash
# FOR TESTING ONLY: a proxy for the image model's calls alone (nothing else uses it), e.g. while testing from a
# machine outside the region where the model is served. Leave it unset in production: the server itself runs
# where the model is served. The status bar and the log say when it is on.
# PANIM_IMAGE_PROXY=http://user:password@proxy.example.com:8080

# The model that writes the free-form Manim figures (empty: the script writer writes them itself). When set, the
# script writer only plans each figure, and this model writes the code of every figure at once (the book's figure
# attached when it rebuilds one); a figure the compiler's run refuses goes back to it with the reason, not to the
# whole section. Pick a strong coding model. PANIM_MANIM_PARALLEL (6): figures written at once.
# PANIM_MANIM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (150): a figure's request with no answer by then is asked once more, then left out.
# PANIM_COMPILE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (600): a compile running longer is stopped and reported.
# PANIM_MANIM_MODEL=

# Speed. Most of a run is the model writing. The transcript is plain teacher's talk: a fast model writes it well
# (the page can override it), and the stronger OPENROUTER_MODEL is kept for the script and its repairs.
# OPENROUTER_TRANSCRIPT_MODEL=google/gemini-3.8-flash
# How hard the model thinks before writing: minimal is fastest; low is the default.
# PANIM_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# How hard it thinks when choosing the video's pictures, diagrams and labels (medium by default: worth it there).
# PANIM_VIDEO_REASONING_EFFORT=medium
# How long the script writer waits for the book's figures to be drawn (seconds from when drawing starts). Figures
# not ready by then are built in Manim this run; their drawings are kept for the next. 0: never wait.
# PANIM_FIGURE_WAIT_SECONDS=120
# Sections written at once (transcript and chapters; at most 8).
# PANIM_TRANSCRIPT_PARALLEL=6
# Pictures a compile makes at once (illustrations, labelled pictures, their labels found); 1: one after another.
# PANIM_IMAGE_PARALLEL=6
# Hand-written Manim blocks test-run at once, and how long each run may take (seconds).
# PANIM_MANIM_CHECK_PARALLEL=4
# PANIM_MANIM_CHECK_SECONDS=120

# Persistence. Without these the pipeline still runs; nothing is written down.
# Schema: harness/supabase/migrations (apply with harness/scripts/apply-schema.sh).
# Save needs the service role key: it writes the tables and the `lectures` bucket. The phone app uses the anon key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://wasvdathkolvobmknkev.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# Whose saved lectures are (created on first save), or a Supabase auth user id in PANIM_OWNER_ID.
# PANIM_OWNER_EMAIL=harness@pocketanim.local

# Only needed if the repo venv is missing; the bridge prefers ../../.venv/bin/python.
PYTHON=

# Optional: clean PDF conversion with figures (https://www.datalab.to). Without it pypdf is used.
DATALAB_API_KEY=
